  "instruction": "Using Visual Studio Code, create a new Python script called walmart_supercenter_trend.py in the /home/user/analysis_results/ directory. Load the dataset 1962_2006_walmart_store_openings.csv, group data by YEAR to calculate the proportion of Supercenters (where type_store equals 'Supercenter') each year, and plot a line chart showing this trend with a ±5% confidence band. Also, create a bar chart showing total store openings per year. Save the first chart as supercenter_trend.png and the second as store_openings_bar.png in the same directory.",
  "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/plotly/datasets/master/1962_2006_walmart_store_openings.csv",

